From 458481bd4cfaee5afe6815927a707557f6fc49bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex native diagnostic <noreply@native-diagnostic.invalid>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:26:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: connect the native diagnostic Ethernet gadget after bind

The native UDC core suppresses the normal post-bind connection for Android,
which enables its gadget later from userspace. The standalone g_ether
diagnostic has no such owner. It registers usb0 and waits for TCP while
MU3D connection_work repeatedly stops at !is_usb_rdy().

Restore the existing gadget connect call after successful bind and UDC
start only for the diagnostic with Ethernet enabled and Android disabled.
The existing pullup callback owns readiness and the controller's normal
role, cable and charging policy. Do not assign readiness or force a role.

This is an assistant-generated native experiment correction, not an
upstream submission. It contains no DCO certification.
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/udc/udc-core.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/udc-core.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/udc-core.c
index bfc6b58..bd5eaf4 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/udc-core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/udc-core.c
@@ -411,6 +411,10 @@ static int udc_bind_to_driver(struct usb_udc *udc, struct usb_gadget_driver *dri
 	 * usb_gadget_connect(udc->gadget);
 	 */
 
+	/* The standalone diagnostic has no Android userspace to connect it. */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MTK_A72_RECOVERY_DISCRIMINATOR) &&
+	    IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_ETH) && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB_G_ANDROID))
+		usb_gadget_connect(udc->gadget);
 
 	kobject_uevent(&udc->dev.kobj, KOBJ_CHANGE);
 	return 0;
